WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome back, everybody.
We are talking

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.834
with Uma Thurman now!

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.667
"Super Pumped:
The Battle for Uber."

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:11.167
You play Arianna Huffington.
-Yes.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.501
-And we were just talking about
that,

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:16.634
and I said, you nailed her
as a character, the voice.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:17.968
You've got the Greek accent.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.734
-I worked on it really hard.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:23.734
But, as you know,
great comedians have nailed it

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.801
and impersonated her better than
I ever will,

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.267
and I knew that too.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:30.200
So, like, I wanted to -- I was
trying to make sure I wasn't,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.667
you know, making a parody of it.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:32.834
-Yeah, you're not doing
an impersonation.

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.334
-She's a brilliant, brilliant,
brilliant woman.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.234
-Oh, yeah.
I mean, but if I did

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.300
Arianna Huffington,
I could do it and be like --

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.667
-I bet you'd do it really well.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:40.701
You want to try?
-Well, it's funny --

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.133
-No, but I would do --
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.434
-But it's a character, and I
would be doing an impersonation.

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:45.000
This is acting.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.234
-It is.
-And it's a real person.

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.534
-And she's a person.
-Yeah.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.501
-You know. With a lot of heart
and a lot of soul

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:55.033
and an incredible mind.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.767
Like, just, like, doing the
research and listening to her,

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:01.467
she has a stronger
working vocabulary than I do.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:04.868
And it's -- I expect more
from myself.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.634
I had to look stuff up.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.300
-Yeah, you had to look stuff up.
-Yeah.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.267
-But did you study, like, all
the TED talks and everything

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:13.734
that she did?
-I looked at all the TED talks.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:19.100
I listened to a lot of her,
kind of, talking spontaneously.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.801
And I was very intrigued that,
actually, she simplifies

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:25.334
her ideas when she has
a planned speech.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.167
-Yeah.
-When she's speaking

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.133
off the cuff,
it's even more complex,

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.467
the sort of imagery and ideas.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.367
You know, just a really
brilliant, brilliant person.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:36.100
-Do you want to tell everybody
what "Super Pumped" is about?

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.634
The a battle for Uber.
-Okay, "Super Pumped" is

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.033
about the battle for Uber.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.901
I mean --
-It's a great story.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.734
-Would you think it was
interesting off the bat?

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:44.734
-No.
-No.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:45.834
-No.
-No.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.868
-No.
-But I was terribly surprised.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.834
-It's a fantastic story.
-It's brilliant.

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:52.501
-It's insane.
-It's kind of like --

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.534
you wouldn't almost believe
it was true.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:57.601
-Yeah, but Arianna was --
-She was asked to go

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.567
onto the board.
-Ah.

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:02.200
-And, so, she sat -- she was
the first woman

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.801
to sit on the board.
And so, it's like,

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.968
a great opportunity,
"Wow, I'm the first woman."

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:11.467
And then it was like,
"I'm the first woman?"

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.067
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.200
Because it kind of went
a little sideways.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.300
-Yeah.
-And particularly around women

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.267
and the treatment of women at
the company,

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.701
which I think was very painful.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.067
But she stayed there working it
through and, you know,

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:27.534
they tried to correct some of
what they had wrong.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:28.901
-Do you Uber?

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.367
-I do Uber.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:34.267
But when I finished the book,
called "Super Pumped,"

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.801
I did download Curb.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:41.033
-Like, as a New Yorker --
-You have to try everything?

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:42.300
-Well, no.
-Oh, cabs.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.100
-I was in New York. Well, one,
it was like, "Ooh,

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.734
this Uber product,
a little bit -- you know."

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.734
Just because it has a label
doesn't mean it's clean.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.901
You know what I mean?
Like, the Ubers themselves

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.033
are not the sketchy part.

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.934
It was more the business
that was sketchy.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.133
But, also I kind of looked out
in New York,

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.767
and this has been
on my mind for a long time.

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.300
Like, we don't want to see
New York stripped

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.801
of our yellow taxis.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.968
-Yeah! We love our yellow cabs.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:10.234
-I mean, they should be, like --
they're part of our heritage.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:11.767
-Yeah, they are.
-So I try to mix it up.

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:14.400
I use different things, but...

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.834
-Shout out to the taxi drivers
out there.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.601
-Shout out to the taxi drivers.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:18.968
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:21.300
Here's Uma Thurman
and Joseph Gordon-Levitt

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.501
in "Super Pumped:
The Battle for Uber."

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:24.601
Take a look.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:27.434
♪♪

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:31.167
-The notorious bad boy of tech.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:34.367
-[ Sighs ] Are you offended by
my "Boober" comment too,

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.033
'cause I'll tell you
what I told my publicist --

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.767
I'm not going on
an apology tour.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.367
-Offended? Darling,
you're talking to someone

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.834
who has had to sit at meals with
Bill Maher

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:48.567
and Pat Buchanan, listen to them
talk, find common ground.

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:51.667
The people who -- thank you --
would take offense

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:52.767
at you crowing a little bit.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.167
Just don't understand.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.167
Every successful person I know
enjoys their success

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:03.033
in their own way or they don't
stay successful very long,

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.667
and they certainly
don't feel it.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:09.634
Now, serving yourself is serving
your company,

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:12.267
which is serving the world.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:13.634
-Nailed it! Come on!

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's how you do it!

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.501
Uma Thurman, everybody,
the one and only.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:21.801
"Super Pumped: The Battle
for Uber" premieres this Sunday

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.801
at 10:00 P.M. on Showtime.

